  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bfcb709b487afd749b8fbd2c4c50e261, type: 3}
  m_Name: Cultist
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: CardDungeon::Assets.Scripts.Heroes.HeroSO
  Key: Cultist
  Label: Cultist
  Blurb: Speaks to things that should not answer. They answer.
  Vision:
    Fantasy: A demon summoner. Planned 2026-10-04 when the old Cultist became the
      Warlock; this is what moved over.
    Role: 'Summoner - brings demons onto the field to fight beside the party. Placeholder:
      Intelligence caster.'
    SignatureMechanic: Adding party members mid-fight (demons). Needs the add/replace-a-party-member
      mechanic, which does not exist yet.
    UltraStyle: Rituals
    Ultras:
    - Name: Sacrifice
      Effect: Sacrifice a target party member, replacing him/her with a demon (demon
        scaled off of the sacrificed party member's stats). Always summoned with
        full health, so a good idea to use when a party member is about to die.
      Unlock: In the demon summoner branch
    Branches:
    - GridBranch: a
      Becomes: A ?? summoner - a bit stronger on its own than a normal branch, to
        justify committing to it.
      IntendedKit: Summon ?? => ?
      Summon: '?'
    Overlaps: 
    OpenQuestions: 'Bare minimum: no grid, not on the party roster, no unlock source
      - it exists only in this window. What happens to a sacrificed hero (dead for
      the fight? revivable? back when the demon leaves)? How long does a demon stay?
      Can he sacrifice himself? Other branches? Stats are placeholders.'
